{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J6qvTBkjxjASp4reSWQAkV","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\t/-\n     2\t# OpenAI's machine model and canonical CNF encoding, copied verbatim\n     3\t\n     4\tThis file is a **verbatim copy of lines 1–190 and 220** of\n     5\t`lean/ComparatorChallenges/SubexponentialSAT.lean` in the OpenAI mathematics\n     6\tcollection (`github.com/openai/math`, commit `4eaee87548250b2682affda7d05d947c05554bae`,\n     7\t2026-10-29; the file's SHA-256 is\n     8\t`4183b2057cff350d66848215ff7167196dfc20e1891b598fdddea59077a76685`), the comparator\n     9\tstatement of family 378, *The Exponential Time Hypothesis is False* (October 25, 2026).\n    10\tLines 191–219, the theorem `exact_count_and_sat` with its `sorry`, are **not** copied: its\n    11\tstatement is restated as the named `Prop` `SubexpCount` in `Frame.lean`, and it is never\n    12\tasserted in this development (loop0014, plan `reports/subexp_pathwidth_plan.md` §0.4.1;\n    13\t`reports/subexp_pathwidth.md` §2).\n    14\t\n    15\tCopyright 2026 OpenAI. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the \"License\"); you\n    16\tmay not use this file except in compliance with the License. You may obtain a copy of the\n    17\tLicense at http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0. Unless required by applicable law or\n    18\tagreed to in writing, software distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\"\n    19\tBASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied. See the\n    20\tLicense for the specific language governing permissions and limitations under the License.\n    21\tThe copy is recorded in `literature/MISSING.md` (the OpenAI collection entry) and the rest of\n    22\tthis development is MIT-licensed as described in the file LICENSE.\n    23\t\n    24\tNothing below is proved: the file contains definitions only (the canonical encoding of a CNF\n    25\tover `Fin n`, the `PrimitiveMachine` multi-tape model over Mathlib's `Turing.TM0.Stmt` and\n    26\t`Turing.Tape`, its `Trace`, the located configuration that monitors the visited cells, and the\n    27\truntime bound `C (L + 1)^d 2^(A · n (log log(n + 16))² / √log(n + 16))`). The namespaces are\n    28\tkept as in the source so that `SubexpCount` reads character for character as the comparator.\n    29\tEverything after this comment block is the copy.\n    30\t-/\n    31\timport Mathlib\n    32\t\n    33\tnamespace OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.BinaryArithmetic\n    34\t\n    35\tdef bitVal (b : Bool) : ℕ := if b then 1 else 0\n    36\t\n    37\tdef toNat : List Bool → ℕ\n    38\t  | [] => 0\n    39\t  | b :: bs => bitVal b + 2 * toNat bs\n    40\t\n    41\tend OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.BinaryArithmetic\n    42\t\n    43\tnamespace OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SAT\n    44\t\n    45\tuniverse u\n    46\t\n    47\tabbrev Assignment (V : Type u) := V → Bool\n    48\t\n    49\tstructure Literal (V : Type u) where\n    50\t  «variable» : V\n    51\t  positive : Bool\n    52\t  deriving DecidableEq\n    53\t\n    54\tabbrev Clause (V : Type u) := Finset (Literal V)\n    55\tabbrev CNF (V : Type u) := Finset (Clause V)\n    56\t\n    57\tvariable {V : Type u} [DecidableEq V]\n    58\t\n    59\tdef Literal.eval (a : Assignment V) (l : Literal V) : Bool :=\n    60\t  a l.variable == l.positive\n    61\t\n    62\tdef Clause.eval (a : Assignment V) (C : Clause V) : Bool :=\n    63\t  decide (∃ l ∈ C, l.eval a = true)\n    64\t\n    65\tdef CNF.eval (a : Assignment V) (F : CNF V) : Bool :=\n    66\t  decide (∀ C ∈ F, C.eval a = true)\n    67\t\n    68\tdef WidthAtMost (k : ℕ) (F : CNF V) : Prop := ∀ C ∈ F, C.card ≤ k\n    69\t\n    70\tsection Finite\n    71\t\n    72\tvariable [Fintype V]\n    73\t\n    74\tdef satisfyingAssignments (F : CNF V) : Finset (Assignment V) :=\n    75\t  Finset.univ.filter fun a => F.eval a = true\n    76\t\n    77\tdef count (F : CNF V) : ℕ := (satisfyingAssignments F).card\n    78\t\n    79\tend Finite\n    80\t\n    81\tend OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SAT\n    82\t\n    83\tnamespace OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Encoding\n    84\t\n    85\tdef encodeNat (n : ℕ) : List Bool := List.replicate n true ++ [false]\n    86\t\n    87\tdef frame (bits : List Bool) : List Bool :=\n    88\t  bits.foldr (fun b rest => true :: b :: rest) [false]\n    89\t\n    90\tdef encodeList {α : Type*} (enc : α → List Bool) : List α → List Bool\n    91\t  | [] => [false]\n    92\t  | a :: as => true :: (frame (enc a) ++ encodeList enc as)\n    93\t\n    94\tdef literalCode {n : ℕ} (l : SAT.Literal (Fin n)) : ℕ :=\n    95\t  2 * l.variable.val + if l.positive then 1 else 0\n    96\t\n    97\tdef clauseNumbers {n : ℕ} (C : SAT.Clause (Fin n)) : List ℕ :=\n    98\t  (C.image literalCode).sort (· ≤ ·)\n    99\t\n   100\tdef cnfNumbers {n : ℕ} (F : SAT.CNF (Fin n)) : List (List ℕ) :=\n   101\t  (F.image clauseNumbers).sort (· ≤ ·)\n   102\t\n   103\tdef encodeCNFBody {n : ℕ} (F : SAT.CNF (Fin n)) : List Bool :=\n   104\t  encodeList (encodeList encodeNat) (cnfNumbers F)\n   105\t\n   106\tdef encodeCNF {n : ℕ} (F : SAT.CNF (Fin n)) : List Bool :=\n   107\t  encodeNat n ++ encodeCNFBody F\n   108\t\n   109\tdef formulaBitLength {n : ℕ} (F : SAT.CNF (Fin n)) : ℕ := (encodeCNF F).length\n   110\t\n   111\tend OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Encoding\n   112\t\n   113\tnamespace OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Computation\n   114\t\n   115\tuniverse u\n   116\t\n   117\tinductive Trace {α : Type u} (step : α → Option α) : ℕ → α → α → Prop\n   118\t  | refl (a : α) : Trace step 0 a a\n   119\t  | cons {n : ℕ} {a b c : α} :\n   120\t      step a = some b → Trace step n b c → Trace step (n + 1) a c\n   121\t\n   122\tstructure PrimitiveMachine where\n   123\t  tapeCount : ℕ\n   124\t  stateCount : ℕ\n   125\t  inputTape : Fin tapeCount\n   126\t  start : Fin stateCount\n   127\t  scan : Fin stateCount → Fin tapeCount\n   128\t  transition : Fin stateCount → Option Bool →\n   129\t    Bool ⊕ (Fin stateCount × Turing.TM0.Stmt (Option Bool))\n   130\t\n   131\tnamespace PrimitiveMachine\n   132\t\n   133\tstructure Cfg (machine : PrimitiveMachine) where\n   134\t  state : Bool ⊕ Fin machine.stateCount\n   135\t  tapes : Fin machine.tapeCount → Turing.Tape (Option Bool)\n   136\t\n   137\tdef step (machine : PrimitiveMachine) (c : machine.Cfg) : Option machine.Cfg :=\n   138\t  match c.state with\n   139\t  | .inl _ => none\n   140\t  | .inr q =>\n   141\t    let tapeIndex := machine.scan q\n   142\t    match machine.transition q (c.tapes tapeIndex).head with\n   143\t    | .inl answer => some ⟨.inl answer, c.tapes⟩\n   144\t    | .inr (q', action) =>\n   145\t      let nextTape :=\n   146\t        match action with\n   147\t        | .move direction => (c.tapes tapeIndex).move direction\n   148\t        | .write symbol => (c.tapes tapeIndex).write symbol\n   149\t      some ⟨.inr q', Function.update c.tapes tapeIndex nextTape⟩\n   150\t\n   151\tdef init (machine : PrimitiveMachine) (input : List Bool) : machine.Cfg :=\n   152\t  ⟨.inr machine.start, fun k =>\n   153\t    if k = machine.inputTape then Turing.Tape.mk₁ (input.map some)\n   154\t    else Turing.Tape.mk₁ []⟩\n   155\t\n   156\tend PrimitiveMachine\n   157\t\n   158\tend OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Computation\n   159\t\n   160\tnamespace OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLog.Statement\n   161\t\n   162\tnoncomputable def runtimeScale (n : ℕ) : ℝ :=\n   163\t  (n : ℝ) * (Real.log (Real.log ((n : ℝ) + 16))) ^ 2 /\n   164\t    Real.sqrt (Real.log ((n : ℝ) + 16))\n   165\t\n   166\tnoncomputable def runtimeBound (constant exponentConstant : ℝ)\n   167\t    (degree inputBits numVars : ℕ) : ℝ :=\n   168\t  constant * ((inputBits : ℝ) + 1) ^ degree *\n   169\t    (2 : ℝ) ^ (exponentConstant * runtimeScale numVars)\n   170\t\n   171\tend OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLog.Statement\n   172\t\n   173\tnamespace OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace\n   174\t\n   175\topen OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Computation\n   176\t\n   177\tdef countWord (a : ℕ) : List Bool := if a = 0 then [false] else a.bits\n   178\t\n   179\tstructure LocatedCfg (machine : PrimitiveMachine) where\n   180\t  config : machine.Cfg\n   181\t  position : Fin machine.tapeCount → ℤ\n   182\t  lower : Fin machine.tapeCount → ℤ\n   183\t  upper : Fin machine.tapeCount → ℤ\n   184\t\n   185\tdef locatedInit (machine : PrimitiveMachine) (input : List Bool) : LocatedCfg machine where\n   186\t  config := machine.init input\n   187\t  position _ := 0\n   188\t  lower _ := 0\n   189\t  upper i := if i = machine.inputTape then Int.ofNat (input.length - 1) else 0\n   190\t\n   191\tdef headDisplacement : Turing.TM0.Stmt (Option Bool) → ℤ\n   192\t  | .move .left => -1\n   193\t  | .move .right => 1\n   194\t  | .write _ => 0\n   195\t\n   196\tdef LocatedCfg.monitor {machine : PrimitiveMachine} (c : LocatedCfg machine)\n   197\t    (config : machine.Cfg) : LocatedCfg machine :=\n   198\t  Sum.elim\n   199\t    (fun _ => { c with config })\n   200\t    (fun q =>\n   201\t      Sum.elim\n   202\t        (fun _ => { c with config })\n   203\t        (fun targetAction =>\n   204\t          let action := targetAction.2\n   205\t          let i := machine.scan q\n   206\t          let position := c.position i + headDisplacement action\n   207\t          { config\n   208\t            position := Function.update c.position i position\n   209\t            lower := Function.update c.lower i (min (c.lower i) position)\n   210\t            upper := Function.update c.upper i (max (c.upper i) position) })\n   211\t        (machine.transition q (c.config.tapes (machine.scan q)).head))\n   212\t    c.config.state\n   213\t\n   214\tdef locatedStep (machine : PrimitiveMachine) (c : LocatedCfg machine) :\n   215\t    Option (LocatedCfg machine) :=\n   216\t  (machine.step c.config).map c.monitor\n   217\t\n   218\tdef visitedSpace {machine : PrimitiveMachine} (c : LocatedCfg machine) : ℕ :=\n   219\t  ∑ i, (c.upper i - c.lower i + 1).toNat\n   220\t\n   221\tend OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f52cb7ed-9351-4bd6-99f1-a93db5c9356a","uuid":"4d1d93c5-acf3-4e17-b502-2a7b3f10a90c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:26:15.735Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"     1\t/-\n     2\t# OpenAI's machine model and canonical CNF encoding, copied verbatim\n     3\t\n     4\tThis file is a **verbatim copy of lines 1–190 and 220** of\n     5\t`lean/ComparatorChallenges/SubexponentialSAT.lean` in the OpenAI mathematics\n     6\tcollection (`github.com/openai/math`, commit `4eaee87548250b2682affda7d05d947c05554bae`,\n     7\t2026-10-29; the file's SHA-256 is\n     8\t`4183b2057cff350d66848215ff7167196dfc20e1891b598fdddea59077a76685`), the comparator\n     9\tstatement of family 378, *The Exponential Time Hypothesis is False* (October 25, 2026).\n    10\tLines 191–219, the theorem `exact_count_and_sat` with its `sorry`, are **not** copied: its\n    11\tstatement is restated as the named `Prop` `SubexpCount` in `Frame.lean`, and it is never\n    12\tasserted in this development (loop0014, plan `reports/subexp_pathwidth_plan.md` §0.4.1;\n    13\t`reports/subexp_pathwidth.md` §2).\n    14\t\n    15\tCopyright 2026 OpenAI. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the \"License\"); you\n    16\tmay not use this file except in compliance with the License. You may obtain a copy of the\n    17\tLicense at http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0. Unless required by applicable law or\n    18\tagreed to in writing, software distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\"\n    19\tBASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied. See the\n    20\tLicense for the specific language governing permissions and limitations under the License.\n    21\tThe copy is recorded in `literature/MISSING.md` (the OpenAI collection entry) and the re